Document Type Declaration

.its an instruction
.tells the web browser which HTML version the page is written in, ensuring that the browser renders the page correctly.
.its not an HTML tag
.not case sensitive

.uses specific rendering mode - helps browser to determine how to display the content of the page
    .standard mode - renders the page according to the modern specifications
    .quirks mode - emulates older browser behavior for compatibility with legacy websites

Without it;
.browsers may enter quirks mode, leading to inconsistent rendering across different browsers.
.rendering issues - CSS properties and layout may not work as intended, causing design problems.
.cross browser inconsistencies - different browsers may interpret the HTML differently, leading to unpredictable results.
.unpredictability - rendering becomes unpredictable, making it difficult for developers to ensure a 
consistent user experience across different browsers and devices.
    .debugging becomes more challenging 
    .avoid deprecated attributes e.g bgcolor, align; use CSS instead 
    